{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q408074","formula":"C₂₁H₂₇NO₄","hill":"C21H27NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":27.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Laudanosine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Laudanosine or N-methyltetrahydropapaverine is a metabolite of the pharmaceutical drugs atracurium and cisatracurium. Laudanosine decreases the seizure threshold, and thus it can induce seizures if present at sufficient threshold concentrations; however, such concentrations are unlikely to be produced consequent to chemodegradable metabolism of clinically administered doses of cisatracurium or atracurium. Laudanosine also occurs naturally in minute amounts (0.1%) in opium, from which it was first isolated in 1871."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":73397,"mass":357.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1CCC2=CC(=C(C=C2[C@@H]1CC3=CC(=C(C=C3)OC)OC)OC)OC","inchikey":"KGPAYJZAMGEDIQ-KRWDZBQOSA-N","iupac":"(1S)-1-[(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)methyl]-6,7-dimethoxy-2-methyl-3,4-dihydro-1H-isoquinoline","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"73397","atoms":53,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":4.008,"y":-1.037,"z":1.408,"el":"O"},{"x":4.047,"y":-1.627,"z":-1.306,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.67,"y":-0.099,"z":-0.153,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.662,"y":-2.688,"z":-0.234,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.604,"y":2.754,"z":-0.248,"el":"N"},{"x":0.322,"y":2.173,"z":0.761,"el":"C"},{"x":1.321,"y":1.157,"z":0.2,"el":"C"},{"x":0.043,"y":2.952,"z":-1.55,"el":"C"},{"x":0.466,"y":1.604,"z":-2.125,"el":"C"},{"x":1.385,"y":0.888,"z":-1.178,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.526,"y":1.509,"z":1.863,"el":"C"},{"x":2.234,"y":0.511,"z":1.051,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.171,"y":4.03,"z":0.206,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.362,"y":0.396,"z":1.305,"el":"C"},{"x":2.292,"y":-0.062,"z":-1.671,"el":"C"},{"x":3.145,"y":-0.422,"z":0.552,"el":"C"},{"x":3.167,"y":-0.715,"z":-0.807,"el":"C"},{"x